verses.tf_en:
① **«قَالُوا اطَّیَّرْنَا بِكَ وَبِمَنْ مَّعَكَ»** (They said: "We consider you and those with you an evil omen!") — Entrenched in pagan superstition, the elite blamed Sayyiduna Salih and his impoverished believers for a local drought and livestock misfortune, declaring them to be a curse (*Tatayyur*)...
② **«قَالَ طٰۤئِرُكُمْ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ»** (He replied: "Your omen is with Allah...") — Firmly refuting superstition: all destinies, bounties, and hardships are decreed by Allah according to His supreme wisdom, not by omens;
③ **«بَلْ اَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تُفْتَنُوْنَ»** (...nay, you are a people being tested!) — Clarifying that their temporal trials were a divine test to expose their corruption and give them cause to reform.
